On the road: a kilometre per hour is the standard in most of the world, while mph rules the US and the UK still use miles per hour on road signs. 1 mph = 1.60934 km/h, so a 70 mph motorway limit is about 113 km/h. To convert mph to km/h, multiply by 1.609; to convert km/h to mph, divide by 1.609 (or multiply by 0.6214). A 100 km/h limit is about 62 mph.

